'' 'dim as V r = p + q' OVER A V WITH NO COPY: fbc casts the value and constructs r from the
'' cast ('operator cast as double', 'constructor( byval as integer )'), measured on fbc-modern
'' 1.20 -- for a variable, an operator's and a call's result, 'var', a 'return', a shared and a
'' field initialiser. tiko copied each (3 for 1 + 2 where fbc prints 4), and the shared one
'' declined (TKO0994). A copy constructor or a string field keeps the copy. See the source.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/cast-ctor-init.bas -o tests/codegen/castctorinit.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/castctorinit.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: shared 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: r1 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: r2 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: r3 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: r4 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: r5 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: r6 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: w 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: D( 4)
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: d2 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: C copy
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: c2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: s2 3
